=== layout: two-panels

# Average 12 and 8 to Get 10

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-two padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
| [ ]{text-align=center} | [White]{text-align=center} | [Blk.R]{text-align=center} |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [White]{text-align=center} | [ ]{text-align=center} | [ ]{text-align=center} |
| [Blk.R]{text-align=center} | [10]{text-align=center} | [ ]{text-align=center} |

White = N.Wh. and S.Wh.

[(12 + 8) / 2 = 10.]{color=#00775F} Each original sequence gets equal weight.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_1.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Step 4: Join the Final Clusters

@left

{table-style=matrix-lower table-group=rhino-two padding="3pt 2pt" font-size=22pt}
| [ ]{text-align=center} | [White]{text-align=center} | [Blk.R]{text-align=center} |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [White]{text-align=center} | [ ]{text-align=center} | [ ]{text-align=center} |
| [Blk.R]{text-align=center} | [10]{text-align=center} | [ ]{text-align=center} |

The root height is 10 / 2 = 5.

The white-rhino branch is 5 - 2 = 3; the black-rhino branch is 5 - 0 = 5.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_2.drawn.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# The Three-Rhino Tree Is Complete

@left

- Each white-rhino tip branch has length 2.
- The white-rhino cluster joins the root with a branch of length 3.
- The black-rhino branch has length 5.
- Every root-to-tip path has length 5.
- The fitted white-to-black path is 10; the original inputs were 12 and 8.

@right

![Rhino example](assets/lect11c_rhino/tree_2.drawn.svg)

